    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "p2p: keep orphan resolution requests for non-witness 1p1c parents",
    "user": {
      "login": "FlashWayne",
      "id": 332458478,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOE9Dp7g",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/332458478?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/FlashWayne",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "When a low-feerate parent is rejected as `TX_RECONSIDERABLE`, `MempoolRejectedTx` calls `m_txrequest.ForgetTxHash(ptx->GetWitnessHash())` (txdownloadman_impl.cpp:473). For a transaction without witness, wtxid == txid, so this also deletes the txid requests that `MaybeAddOrphanResolutionCandidate` queued for every peer that announced the orphan child.\r\n\r\nIf the parent then comes from a peer that did not announce the child:\r\n\r\n- `Find1P1CPackage` only pairs the parent with children from the same peer, so no package is formed\r\n- the child's announcers are never asked for the parent\r\n- the child stays in the orphanage until some new peer announces it\r\n\r\nWith a segwit parent the txid differs from the wtxid, so the txid requests survive and the package gets accepted. A legacy (P2PK) parent is affected.\r\n\r\nThis skips `ForgetTxHash` when the result is `TX_RECONSIDERABLE` and the tx has no witness. New wtxid announcements of that parent are still ignored through `AlreadyHaveTx(include_reconsiderable=true)`. The cost is that announcements already queued may download the parent once more.\r\n\r\nThe new `test_parent_from_other_peer` in `p2p_opportunistic_1p1c.py` runs for a segwit and a legacy parent: peer A sends the child (orphan), peer B sends the low-fee parent, then it checks that A is asked for the parent by txid and the package is accepted. On master the legacy case times out waiting for that request; with the change it passes. `p2p_orphan_handling.py` and `p2p_tx_download.py` still pass.\r\n",
