      "message": "p2p: keep orphan resolution requests for non-witness 1p1c parents\n\nWhen a low-feerate parent is rejected as TX_RECONSIDERABLE, the tx\ndownload manager calls m_txrequest.ForgetTxHash(wtxid). For a tx without\nwitness, wtxid == txid, so this also deletes the txid requests that were\nqueued to resolve an orphan child from the peers that announced it.\n\nIf the parent arrives from a peer that didn't announce the child,\nFind1P1CPackage doesn't pair them (it only considers children from the\nsame peer), and the child's announcers are never asked for the parent. The\nchild stays in the orphanage until some new peer announces it. With a\nsegwit parent the txid differs from the wtxid, so the requests survive.\n\nSkip ForgetTxHash for a reconsiderable tx that has no witness. New wtxid\nannouncements are still ignored through AlreadyHaveTx.",
